below 70 with D below 3.38 all failed geometry or were dominated. The remaining hypervolume comes only from filling gaps in the sweep, and the gaps are small. I do that here, plus two tiny D probes and one gamma probe right at the g cap.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-42e1b7d95981 (gamma -1.5) and C-c2d1addc0c7e (-1.75) leave a 0.25 deg gap; C-760c0b324dc5 (-1.95) to C-8438a428eb66 (-2.2) leaves another 0.25 deg gap.\",\"Smaller gaps remain between -2.35 and -2.5 (C-8dd96d9f9b80, C-e7776fa4dd93), -2.6 and -2.75 (C-e80bd3e93def, C-f402f187ca09), -2.83 and -2.95, and -3.05 and -3.2 (C-b16616085f94, C-7dcb5a130823).\",\"C-746e99b64989 at gamma -3.5701 has max_g margin 2.5e-5, which leaves ~1.5e-4 deg of headroom (max_g slope ~1.7 g/deg).\",\"Mass-fraction margin vs D: 3.383 -> 1.3e-3, 3.385 -> 1.4e-4, 3.3852 -> 3e-6 to 2.7e-5. A linear estimate puts zero margin near D~3.38525.\",\"Geometry failures C-4aa35af3d6a3, C-39bfab3c832b and C-fb6ea8c7e775 (bluntness 1.205-1.21) show that bluntness above 1.2 is outside the surrogate hull, so I leave bluntness and cone at 1.2 and 70.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Flux and bondline temperature trade off through gamma. A steeper entry raises peak flux (~20-24 kW/m2 per deg) and lowers bondline temperature (~10-16 K per deg) by shortening the heat pulse. g rises with steepness and caps at about -3.57 deg. The front is smooth and slowly curving, so interpolating linearly between neighbouring rows gives reliable predictions, and each new gap point adds a small sliver of dominated area. The relations between D, flux and mass fraction come from the tables plus prior knowledge that flux ~ 1/sqrt(nose radius).\",\"uncertainty\":\"Gains are tiny (order 1e-4 in normalised hypervolume). D probes near 3.38523 may break the mass-fraction limit, because the true parent D values are hidden by rounding. The gamma=-3.5702 probe may exceed max_g. Predicted values are linear interpolations, accurate to about 0.2% on flux and about 0.2 K on temperature. No higher-fidelity check is requested.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-42e1b7d95981\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229210,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.25,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a non-dominated point in the widest front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-42e1b7d95981\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230220,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.44,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a non-dominated point in the widest front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-42e1b7d95981\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231224,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.63,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds a non-dominated point in the widest front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-760c0b324dc5\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.97 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237590,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.23 deg gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-760c0b324dc5\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.97 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":238700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a 0.23 deg gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8438a428eb66\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between